&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;London, UK – Hybrid (2 days per week in office)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With millions of diners, 70,000+ restaurant partners and 25+ years of experience, OpenTable, part of Booking Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ: BKNG), is an industry leader with a passion for helping restaurants thrive. Our world-class technology empowers restaurants to focus on what matters most – their team, their guests, and their bottom line – while enabling diners to discover and book the perfect restaurant for every occasion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every employee at OpenTable has a tangible impact on what we do and how we do it. You’ll also be part of a global team that includes and its portfolio of metasearch brands. Hospitality is all about taking care of others, and it defines our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;OpenTable is looking for a highly motivated, practical, and business-oriented Senior Counsel, Privacy &amp;amp; Product to join our Legal team. You will serve as a trusted advisor to OpenTable’s Product, Engineering, Security, Commercial, Partnerships, and Marketing teams, providing strategic and practical counsel across product development, privacy and data protection, artificial intelligence, information security, consumer protection, and related regulatory matters. You will also serve as OpenTable’s Deputy Privacy Officer, helping lead and operationalize OpenTable’s global privacy program and serving as a key liaison with Booking Holdings, Inc. (BHI) on privacy and data protection matters. This role is ideal for a lawyer who enjoys working closely with commercial, product and technical teams, navigating emerging areas of law, and developing practical solutions that enable responsible innovation at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary legal partner to OpenTable’s Product, Engineering, Security, Commercial, Partnerships, and Marketing teams, providing end-to-end counseling on new products, features, data uses, integrations, consumer experiences, and other strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Deputy Privacy Officer for OpenTable, helping lead and operationalize OpenTable’s global privacy program and serving as a key liaison with BHI on privacy strategy, governance, regulatory developments, and group-wide privacy initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on global privacy and data protection requirements and embed privacy-by-design principles into OpenTable’s products and operations, including counseling on data collection, use, sharing, retention, consent, personalization, and consumer rights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic legal guidance on the development, deployment, procurement, and use of artificial intelligence and emerging technologies, including generative AI and AI-powered product features, and help develop scalable AI governance frameworks as the regulatory landscape evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic legal advice and guidance to Product teams regarding product development, launch, and sunsetting, with strong focus on legal risks related to data privacy, cybersecurity, data usage and ownership, consumer protection, and marketing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with OpenTable’s Information Security team on cybersecurity and data security matters, including product and vendor security risk, security requirements, incident response, potential data breaches, regulatory obligations, and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and address emerging product, privacy, AI, security, consumer protection, and regulatory risks; draft and negotiate related agreements and terms; and develop scalable legal processes, policies, playbooks, and disclosures that enable the business to innovate responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant legal experience, including significant experience advising on privacy, data protection, technology, and product matters, preferably in-house at a technology, consumer, marketplace, or other high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;J.D. from an accredited U.S. law school and active membership in good standing in at least one U.S. state bar, or equivalent legal qualification and authorization to practice law in the United Kingdom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of U.S. and global privacy and data protection laws, including GDPR and U.S. state privacy laws, as well as global consumer protection laws, with demonstrated experience translating complex legal and regulatory requirements into practical product and business guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience providing product counseling, including partnering directly with Product and Engineering teams on new products, features, data uses, and technology initiatives from development through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or helping lead a global privacy program, including privacy governance, policies, compliance frameworks, and cross-functional implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on information security and cybersecurity matters, including security requirements, incident response, and related regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment, communication, and stakeholder-management skills, with demonstrated ability to assess risk, navigate ambiguity, and provide practical advice to cross-functional teams and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on artificial intelligence and emerging technologies, including legal and regulatory considerations associated with developing, deploying, or procuring AI-enabled products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within a complex global organization or corporate group and partnering effectively with enterprise-level legal, privacy, security, compliance, or governance functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CIPP/US, CIPP/E, CIPM, AIGP, or similar privacy or AI certification preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 weeks paid vacation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private health &amp;amp; dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from (almost) anywhere for up to 20 days per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on mental health and well-being:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid therapy sessions through SpringHealth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid subscription to Headspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company-wide week off a year - the whole team fully recharges (and returns without a pile-up of work!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off for your birthday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid volunteer time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on your career growth:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development Dollars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to thousands of on-demand e-learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel Discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Income protection and life assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program - including 24/7 GP &amp;amp; free legal advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discounted gym membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bike2Work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Season ticket loan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events &amp;amp; Thursday happy hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch 2 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best connections happen face-to-face, whether you’re sitting down to dinner or having coffee with a coworker. That’s why OpenTable has adopted a hybrid workplace model. This role aligns with that approach, with an expectation of coming into the office two days a week—giving employees the best of both worlds: in-person collaboration and flexibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment &amp;amp; Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At OpenTable, we pride ourselves on fostering a global and dynamic work environment. As a team member with us, you will benefit from a schedule tailored to accommodate a global workforce operating across multiple time zones. While the majority of your responsibilities may align with conventional business hours, there will be instances where you are expected to manage communications - via calls, Slack messages, or emails - outside of regular working hours to effectively collaborate with international colleagues, respond to restaurant partners, and/or address urgent matters. OpenTable will always abide by and consider local laws and regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels they belong and can thrive. We know the best ideas come when we bring different voices to the table, so we&#39;re building a team as dynamic as the diners and restaurants we serve—and fostering a culture where everyone feels welcome to be themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any reasonable adjustments during the application/interview process, or on the job, we’re here to support you. Please reach out to your recruiter to request any accommodations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-BR1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;About Dwelly&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dwelly is building the AI operating system for residential lettings. Its growing network of agencies provides its AI with real-world data, continuous feedback, and control over complete workflows, making exceptional service the standard for landlords and tenants. Today, Dwelly operates more than 15,000 properties and $470 million in GMV, making it one of the UK’s ten largest lettings operators. The company has raised $263 million.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re a fast-growing, product-focused company, backed by top-tier investors and led by a team with deep experience in real estate, technology, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note this role sits with Helen Breeze Property Management, Sevenoaks, Dwelly&#39;s Agency.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced Senior Block Manager / Block Management Team Leader to join our bespoke managing agent based in Sevenoaks, covering the West Kent area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a key role within the business, with overall responsibility for a specialist block-management team of four — two property managers and two accounts administrators — together with oversight of a portfolio of approximately 50 residential blocks, none exceeding 18 metres in height.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity for an experienced Block Manager to take a genuine leadership role within a growing business, providing technical and operational leadership to the team, acting as a point of escalation for complex matters, and having direct involvement in key business decisions and future growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, support and develop a team of two Property Managers and two Accounts Administrators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the day-to-day planning and operation of the block-management department&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance, support and workload management to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain overall oversight of a portfolio of approximately 50 residential blocks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the principal point of escalation for complex property, leaseholder and client matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee service-charge budgets, financial management and accounts across the portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accounts are prepared accurately and delivered within agreed timescales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set, monitor and review departmental KPIs and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide monthly management reports to senior management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards of customer service and client communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee compliance and health &amp;amp; safety requirements across the portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure appropriate action is taken where compliance or maintenance issues are identified&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team with major works, contractor management and other complex property matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership and direction while remaining hands-on and accessible to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to wider business strategy, operational improvements and future growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For (Essential)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years&#39; experience in private residential leasehold/block management, covering service charge budgets, service charge accounts, major works, Section 20, leasehold legislation, contractor management, compliance, health &amp;amp; safety, and the Building Safety Act&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong practical experience managing residential block portfolios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of leasehold and service-charge management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing budgets, accounts and financial matters associated with managed properties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good working knowledge of the Building Safety Act and relevant building safety requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of compliance and health &amp;amp; safety within residential property management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational and time-management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and client-management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal confidently with complex or escalated matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clean UK driving licence and access to your own vehicle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TPI/IRPM qualification or equivalent professional qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous supervisory or team-management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or developing Property Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with major works and Section 20 consultation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial block-management experience and ready to take a first formal team-leadership role will also be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary: &lt;/strong&gt;£48,000–£55,000 per year&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits: &lt;/strong&gt;Company events, company pension, free parking, work from home&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is it like being a Dwell-er?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feel free to check out &lt;a href=&quot;https://docsend.com/view/7v8gwrjaky7mn895&quot;&gt;Dwelly Core Principles&lt;/a&gt;. That’s about what we believe in, how we operate and make decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we offer is not a fancy office or a static workplace. Instead, this is solving one of worlds’ most complex problems in the largest consumer industry in the world (residential rentals), to improve the experience for &amp;gt;30% of households (&amp;gt;5M in the UK, and &amp;gt;100M including EU and US) that live in rental homes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is about disrupting the largest, most antiquated industry in the world, with one of the strongest operational and technical teams that exist in the UK and the EU. We work hard, and we shoot for extremely ambitious results. But we want people to be proud of what they’ve built and be able to look back and say one day “hell yeah, that was me that did it all”.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession rather than competitive focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for invention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;556&quot; data-end=&quot;829&quot;&gt;By applying for this position, you consent to the processing and storage of your personal data for recruitment purposes for up to 365 days, in accordance with our data retention policy and applicable data protection laws.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Pallet &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Pallet is building AI Agents to transform the physical economy — a $12 trillion global industry. We’ve raised $50M from top investors, including General Catalyst, Bessemer Venture Partners, and Bain Capital Ventures. In under two years, we’ve achieved 700% revenue growth and are just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Our mission is to increase the efficiency of the global supply chain by automating the manual workflows that slow supply chain teams down — from scheduling and appointment setting to data entry and load management. Our flagship platform provides end-to-end visibility, control, and optimization, while our newest product, CoPallet, introduces AI Agents that can understand and execute requests in real time and integrate directly with customer systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;As companies across the physical economy look to generative AI to drive efficiency, many are turning to Pallet to lead the way. With deep supply chain expertise and cutting-edge AI capabilities, we’re positioned to build the next $10B company powering the physical economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and work alongside leaders from Google, DoorDash, YC, and more to shape the future of supply chain technology.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London, United Kingdom or Zurich, Switzerland (Remote to start, transitioning to 5 days/week in-office once our local office opens)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You could be an Enterprise Account Executive anywhere. Why us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a well-funded, high-growth startup on a clear path to $100M ARR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell a category-defining AI Agents platform with massive surface area across logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Pallet’s presence across Europe as one of the first commercial hires on the ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with founders and senior leadership to define our international go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help transform one of the world’s largest industries while building toward a $10B+ outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring our first Enterprise Account Executives in EMEA to build Pallet’s commercial presence across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own net-new enterprise acquisition across the region, build relationships with the largest logistics providers in Europe, and help establish the playbook for our international expansion. This is a highly consultative enterprise sales role focused on educating customers on an entirely new category of AI-powered workflow automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with Sales, Product, Engineering, Solutions, and Customer Success to drive a solution-selling motion centered around workflow discovery, AI use case identification, structured pilots, and measurable ROI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Initially, this role will be remote from London while we establish our UK presence. Once our London office opens, this role will transition to working from the office five days per week when not traveling to customer sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full enterprise sales cycle across EMEA, from outbound prospecting through contract signature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a 3x-4x qualified pipeline through disciplined outbound execution while self-sourcing at least 30% of opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders across Europe’s largest logistics providers, including COO, CIO, VP Operations, VP Supply Chain, and VP Technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead consultative discovery sessions that map operational workflows to Pallet’s AI agent capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and lead structured pilots that demonstrate measurable operational ROI and convert into enterprise deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive business cases that align operational improvements with financial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document repeatable customer use cases and market feedback to shape Pallet’s product roadmap and international GTM strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish Pallet as the leading AI platform for enterprise logistics across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of enterprise B2B SaaS or enterprise logistics sales experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-fluent Spanish you can run discovery, negotiate and present to executives in Spanish.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of consistently closing six- and seven-figure enterprise software agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative selling and value-based sales methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating complex buying committees and long enterprise sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence with senior operators and technology leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable selling technical, workflow-heavy software products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly understand complex logistics operations and translate them into compelling AI automation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent outbound prospecting and territory-building discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel extensively across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience selling into logistics, supply chain, transportation, or warehouse operations is strongly preferred but not required. Candidates without logistics experience should demonstrate an ability to quickly learn operational workflows and become trusted advisors to customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working hours are generally &lt;strong&gt;9:00am-6:00pm London time&lt;/strong&gt;, providing full coverage of the European business day while maintaining regular collaboration with our San Francisco headquarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll typically spend:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mornings and early afternoons working directly with European customers and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Late afternoons collaborating with our US-based Sales, Product, and Engineering teams during our daily overlap window.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 75% of your time traveling across Europe for customer meetings, executive workshops, pilots, and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Initially this role will be remote. Once Pallet opens its local office, you’ll work from the office five days per week whenever you’re not traveling to customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll report directly to the &lt;strong&gt;General Manager, London&lt;/strong&gt; for territory strategy, customer relationships, and international expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also work closely with our &lt;strong&gt;Head of Sales&lt;/strong&gt;, participating in weekly pipeline reviews, forecasting, and sales process alignment with the US team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chat with Christy - Business Recruiter - 30 mins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deal Review - 30 mins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discovery Mock Interview - 45-60 mins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final Interview - ~3 hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief Background Check and Reference Check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast, and we’ll keep you informed at every stage of the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The estimated compensation range for this role is &lt;strong&gt;£100,000-£240,000 OTE&lt;/strong&gt;, depending on experience and skill set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compensation follows a standard 50/50 enterprise sales structure consisting of base salary and target commission. High performers are eligible for uncapped commission accelerators above quota.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to cash compensation, we offer competitive equity, benefits, and significant growth opportunities as one of our earliest international commercial hires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Final compensation will be determined based on experience, qualifications, and demonstrated enterprise sales performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people the same way we invest in our product: seriously.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🩺 Health, Vision, and Dental benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏝️ Take-what-you-need Paid Vacation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;➕ Life Insurance and Accidental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;❤️‍🩹 Short-Term Disability Coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 Generous salary and equity for all staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🪜 401k option; helping you save for the future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🧑‍🧑‍🧒‍🧒 Paid parental leave to support growing families&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📚 Yearly learning and development stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚌 Commuter benefits for Bay Area employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚘 Uber ride stipend if you ever have to work late in the office&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏡 Remote office home stipend to get you comfy in your space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🍔 Daily catered lunches provided&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;✈️ Onboarding trip to San Francisco HQ if you work remotely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🥤 Monthly happy hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎉 Annual Company Offsites; our last one was in Palm Springs CA 🌴&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an in-person company. Our offices in San Francisco, New York City and London are where ideas get built, decisions get made, and the team gets stronger. We have invested in making them genuinely great places to spend your day, with catered lunches, monthly happy hours, and people who care about the work and each other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most of our team works in office five days a week. For select roles, we hire remotely across the U.S. Remote employees come to one of our offices for their first week to onboard and meet the team, and we cover the full trip.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every role is different. Travel expectations are always shared upfront in the job description and confirmed in your first call with us.&lt;/p&gt;
